From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] bsd: export file_offset_get and file_offset_set

A kext that reads or writes a process's descriptor through its vnode
(file_vnode_withvid() and vn_rdwr(), the only KPI for it) passes vn_rdwr()
an explicit offset, and can neither learn where the process's own read(2)
and write(2) left the descriptor nor move it past what the kext
transferred. zfs.kext's zfs receive reads a stream from the descriptor
after libzfs has read its BEGIN record itself, and zfs send writes after
libzfs's own headers (-R); the macOS layer's SPL starts every descriptor
at offset 0, so zfs receive < file failed with "invalid backup stream"
(OpenZFS test suite, P3-01 checkpoint 2). On FreeBSD and Linux the module
uses and advances the descriptor's offset. Two BSD KPI functions give a
kext the same: file_offset_get() and file_offset_set() read and set the
offset of a vnode descriptor of the current process (fg_offset, as
lseek(2) would), and BSDKernel.exports exports them. zfs.kext's SPL uses
them in getf() and releasefp() (kexts/zfs/patches/0005), the pairing
docs/architecture/filesystems.md §2 asks for.

Rebase-risk: low (two new functions, two export names).
---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_descrip.c b/bsd/kern/kern_descrip.c
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_descrip.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_descrip.c
@@ -2125,10 +2125,62 @@
 		if (vidp) {
 			*vidp = vnode_vid((struct vnode *)fp_get_data(fp));
 		}
+	}
+	return error;
+}
+
+/*
+ * NeoDarwin: file_offset_get, file_offset_set
+ *
+ * Description:	Get or set the file offset of a vnode descriptor of the
+ *		current process: for a kext that does I/O on the descriptor's
+ *		vnode on the process's behalf (vn_rdwr() takes an explicit
+ *		offset) and must start where the process's read(2) or
+ *		write(2) left off, and leave the offset after what it
+ *		transferred, as the descriptor's own I/O would. zfs.kext's
+ *		zfs send and zfs receive do (P3-01, its SPL's getf()).
+ *
+ * Returns:	0				Success
+ *		EINVAL				The fd does not refer to a
+ *						vnode fileproc entry
+ *	fp_lookup:EBADF				Bad file descriptor
+ */
+int file_offset_get(int fd, off_t *offp);
+int file_offset_set(int fd, off_t off);
+
+int
+file_offset_get(int fd, off_t *offp)
+{
+	proc_t p = current_proc();
+	struct fileproc *fp;
+	int error;
+
+	error = fp_get_ftype(p, fd, DTYPE_VNODE, EINVAL, &fp);
+	if (error == 0) {
+		*offp = fp->fp_glob->fg_offset;
+		fp_drop(p, fd, fp, 0);
 	}
 	return error;
 }
 
+int
+file_offset_set(int fd, off_t off)
+{
+	proc_t p = current_proc();
+	struct fileproc *fp;
+	int error;
+
+	if (off < 0) {
+		return EINVAL;
+	}
+	error = fp_get_ftype(p, fd, DTYPE_VNODE, EINVAL, &fp);
+	if (error == 0) {
+		fp->fp_glob->fg_offset = off;
+		fp_drop(p, fd, fp, 0);
+	}
+	return error;
+}
+
 /*
  * file_socket
  *
diff --git a/config/BSDKernel.exports b/config/BSDKernel.exports
--- a/config/BSDKernel.exports
+++ b/config/BSDKernel.exports
@@ -201,6 +201,8 @@
 _fifo_write
 _file_drop
 _file_flags
+_file_offset_get
+_file_offset_set
 _file_socket
 _file_vnode_withvid
 _fubyte
